---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Callout from "../components/Callout.astro";
---
<Layout title="Legal & privacy" path="/legal/" description="SentinelCore license, terms, and privacy policy. No telemetry; the email relay explained.">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1>Legal &amp; privacy</h1>

      <h2>License &amp; terms</h2>
      <p>
        SentinelCore is distributed under its project license (All Rights Reserved unless stated
        otherwise in the release). Use is permitted only on networks you own or are explicitly
        authorized to monitor and defend. The software is provided “as is”, without warranty of any
        kind; you are responsible for how and where you deploy it.
      </p>

      <h2>Privacy policy</h2>
      <Callout tone="ok" title="No telemetry, no trackers">
        The software collects no usage analytics and phones home for nothing. This website uses no
        analytics or third-party trackers.
      </Callout>
      <p>
        All operational data — captured traffic, flows, uploaded PCAPs, events, incidents, reports —
        stays on your host. SentinelCore has exactly one optional outbound dependency: the email relay.
      </p>
      <h3>What the email relay receives</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Your verified admin email address (the only permitted recipient).</li>
        <li>The subject and rendered body of notifications you choose to send.</li>
        <li>A per-install token (stored only as a hash; revocable at any time).</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>What it never receives</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Network traffic, PCAPs, flows, events, incidents or reports.</li>
        <li>Any mail-provider key — none exists on your box.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Contact &amp; support</h2>
      <p>
        For support, questions or security reports, contact the SentinelCore team through the channel
        provided with your release. Please report suspected vulnerabilities privately rather than in
        public issues.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .narrow { max-width: 760px; }
  h2 { margin-top: 2rem; }
  h3 { margin-top: 1.2rem; }
  ul { color: rgb(var(--text-muted)); padding-left: 1.2rem; }
  li { margin-bottom: 0.35rem; }
</style>
